      "patternId": "n6-research-and-data-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-81.t05",
      "en": "There was a slight rise in the number of cyclists.",
      "es": "Hubo una ligera subida en el número de ciclistas.",
      "explanationEs": "Slight rise es un cambio pequeño; para uno grande se usaría big o sharp.",
      "segments": [
        "There was a slight rise",
        "in the number of cyclists."
      ],
      "audioText": "There was a slight rise in the number of cyclists.",
      "audioMode": "tts",
      "languageCode": "en",
      "patternId": "n6-research-and-data-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "en.n6.class-81.t06",
      "en": "A small minority said no, and that figure fell from 20 percent to 12 percent.",
      "es": "Una pequeña minoría dijo que no, y esa cifra bajó del 20 al 12 por ciento.",
      "explanationEs": "Minority es menos de la mitad. Fell es el pasado de fall: indica una bajada.",
      "segments": [
